      "type": "User",
      "user_view_type": "public",
      "site_admin": false
    },
    "body": "Thanks for the review @davidkna! I just pushed a refactor:\r\n\r\n- Reused `exec_git`: Added a new `Repo::open_bare` helper. Since YADM uses `$HOME` as a work-tree instead of the `current_dir`, this lets us build a standalone repo and fully reuse `exec_git` without duplicating the timeout/fsmonitor logic.\r\n\r\n- Shared utilities: Extracted a `is_dirty_or_ahead` helper in `git_status.rs` that reuses the existing `RepoStatus` porcelain v2 parser. No more duplicated parsing logic.\r\n\r\n- Regarding `is_dirty()`: I kept the single `git` subprocess path for maximum simplicity right now to avoid logic drift. I'm happy to add a `gix` fast path in a follow up PR if you'd prefer.\r\n\r\nLet me know if this looks good to you.",
